Yes, I got it running on an AXP 3000-800S without too many differences 
from an Ultrix installation.  The configuration scripts, etc. worked 
well.
There was one little problem, though, that took me a while to narrow 
down.  the inews program wasn't connecting to the server and would spool a 
posted message to be sent later by rnews.  The problem turned up in the 
innsource/lib/remopen.c file in the NNTPconnect procedure.
I think the problem arose because we use an alias name for our server 
(news.spu.edu).
Anyway, when the returned value from the inet_addr() call (an unsigned 
long) is tested for the if statement, the != is not evaluated correctly.  
In our case, the returned value was really -1 (a printf with %lX showed 
all F's).  But since an unsigned long is much larger on the Alpha 
architecture, it didn't look like it overflowed and created the -1, 
instead it looked like a normal (albeit huge) number.  This effectively 
caused a later call to connect() to fail and the whole procedure 
returned a -1 error.  Since my C programming isn't the best and I've 
spent enough time on this already, I "fixed" it for us by commenting out 
the test and making it "if (0)" as you can see.
If someone knows how to fix this properly, I'd be glad to hear about it.

Other than that, no major headaches...


