This is a bug in xdm on DEC OSF/1 V1.3.  Either upgrade to V2.0 (recently
released) or else get the patch kit known as OSF1_V13_PATCH001.tar from your
Customer Support Center.  This patch kit fixes a great many X-related problems,
but, of course, all the fixes are also in V2.0.

The problem with xdm is an open file descriptor.  The problem appears after
about 50 logins.  To temporarily cure the problem without rebooting, you can
stop and restart xdm like this:

	# /sbin/init.d/xdm stop
	# /sbin/init.d/xdm start
