Finally !!  I was able to build an executable with no pipe bugs!

Key #1 - using xmkmf as suggested by Peter Derr (thanks!) and not
following the usual method using the Makefile (yes, that was suggested
in the README's..... that'll teach me!  But being new to doing alot of 
this type of thing, I have never used Imake before.)

However, I did have to do the following steps exactly in order:

 - untar latest version (for a fresh start after all my failed attempts...)
 - copy config/config.osf1 to config.h
 - xmkmf
 - make depend   (which may spit out an error... thats ok)
 - make clean
 - make

I hope this helps all the others who mailed me "me too"-type messages!

And thanks to my friend Gary who made use of DEC's axposf system 
for alot of testing!  (  Gary:  go buy your own Alpha...  ;-)  )


