Hi All:

This may be old news but I thought I might toss this in on
the outside chance someone is having the same sort of problems.

I recently installed LPS17 printservers on our Alpha.  The actual
printers were on a different subnet from the Alpha.

The software installation went pretty routinely, and the instructions
which come with the distribution strongly advises to use the 'quickstart'
steps to bring up the first printer.  All the examples given are for
printserver20's.

After checking and rechecking my installation, I was at a loss to
explain why the LPS17 would begin its boot load, but stop
loading after 98% of the file had been brought across.  The display
on the printer said VAXELN V4.2 LPS.  I called tech support and
we began trying to figure out what was wrong.

The solution turned out to be a little tricky. (Not difficult, just
obscure until you understand the why's and wherefores)

In one of the steps you are to copy lps_printserver.sys into the
tftpboot directory.  This is okay if your running an LPS20 printer.

If your running a LPS17 printer you should copy lps_printserver17.sys
into this directory.  The reason the lps17 was not loading the full
lps image was that it was expecting a shorter load.  Mystery solved.

We also ran into a problem with providing the default gateway address,
which was to a cisco MGS box.  For some reason the printer wouldn't
use this address, and we ended up changing the default mask from
255.255.255.0 to 255.255.0.0 before the printer would finally complete
its load.

We have only one outstanding problem.  With three printers available,
for some reason, one of the printers gets a FILTERS error, even after
reinstalling its print manager from scratch.  More work.

Goodluck installing your LPS, and I hope this helped someone

Rich Knowles              knowles@fnalv.fnal.gov



