Tony,
I just tested a short program using DEC Cxx. 
#include <stdio.h>
int main()
{
        printf("sizeof long%ld, sizeof int:%ld\n", sizeof(long), sizeof(int));
}
sauron:test/qar/library {898%} a.out
sizeof long8, sizeof int:4

I did test on both V2.0 system and a V1.3 system. Also, a comparison of 2
pointers should never be converted to arithmetic types. (Refer to ANSI
3.3.8). I think that the version of CXX on the V1.3 system I tested on was
the released version of DEC CXX. I do know that the version on my V2.0
system is not yet released.
