If you've got stuff that must run, uninterrupted for weeks, you should have
more than checkpoints going on:

1) UPS UPS UPS.  power failures should NOT be an issue if you have critical
systems.

2) Live backups can be done handily with mirroring software.  That is, mirror
your disk to another so that they're written to identically.  "Break the
mirror", so that you're no longer mirroring.  Backup the mirror disk.  Not
necessarily an inexpensive way to backup a home system, but in a mission-
critical environment, I would expect something like this to be in place.

