What you can do is probably to tell your motif applications to
use the "Delete" key for what it is intended for (delete previous),
with the following X resources:

*XmText.translations: #override\n\
      <Key>osfDelete: delete-previous-character() \n\
      <Key>Delete: delete-previous-character()
*XmTextField.translations: #override\n\
      <Key>osfDelete: delete-previous-character() \n\
      <Key>Delete: delete-previous-character()

I have totally failed to understand why you need both 'osfDelete' and
'Delete', but it works with this - even on Sun/HP boxes.

Personally, I think this is one of the stupidest GRD's that has ever
been, since it's such an arbitrary choice. Thankfully, with the leeway
xmodmap and X translations offer, you can mostly have it both ways
nowadays. I prefer using Delete the 'DEC way' and never use backspace
(other than as a Help key in emacs), and I configure all our machines
and applications that way. As long as it's consistent, everybody's
happy :-)

 - Arne H. Juul


