>1. bitnet addresses through a gateway at vmcms.csuohio.edu
>2. addresses of this format: name%taonode@vmcms.csuohio.edu
	Hi,
	 I thought I was the only one :-). 
  I've made about 4 manual patches to the DEC supplied sendmail.cf, after
  the M4 macro processing stage. I had thought that this was due to our
  strange setup, but I have had bounces from several OSF/1 machines with
  this specific problem.
   	I enclose my fix to sendmail.cf. Usual as-is no-warranties apply.
  
------from.my.sendmail.cf.use.at.own.risk---------
##### special local conversions (exit path from S3)
S7
# atp 1994 repeated use of %->@ in S3 (R$+%$+) on a name already
#	   containing an @ (atp%mssly1.mssl.ucl.ac.uk@ucl.ac.uk)
#	   causes a rewrite error in S9 
#	   so has to be undone here (defocus back to one)
R$*<@$+<@$+>>$*		$1%$2<@$3>$4			undo damage in S3
R$*<@$+%$+>$*		$1%$2<@$3>$4			move @ right after %
R$+<@POP>$*		$@$1<@POP>$2			POP already OK
R$*<@$->$*		$@$1<@$2.$N>$3			qualify hostnames

-----end.of.extract------

	Note extra line. I can't remember details about this now, 
  (sendmail does tend to have a small memory-retention half-life), but
  there was a reason for not fixing this by putting a $: in the offending
  ruleset 3 rewriting rule. 

	share+enjoy

		Andy Phillips

