>from VMS, you will really notice this.

The problem with find-based backups is that they don't know to take
everything below new or renamed directories.  And incrementals in
general have the problem that if you restore a chain of them you
accumulate all the files that existed at the times they were taken
even though they may have been subsequently deleted.  GNUtar makes
an attempt to address these problems with the --listed-incremental
option, but it is unfortuantely badly documented.

