All this is merely NOT a problem of the PS Viewer but of the XServer.
The DPS extension of certain servers seems to be not too stable, I had
XServer crashes, too. The 0.7 scale problem has nothing at all to do with
4.2 (as I have it with 4.3 f.i.), but with the limitation of the PX*
XServers to be unable to allocate any pixmap larger than the screen, which
kicks out every program which trys to provide buffered PS rendering.

|>  SO: Is there a PosScript viewer out there that actually works?
|>Ghoscript seems to work but not ghostview. Did somebody port it?
|>Or is there a real fix to dxview (or I messed up something during
|>installation?

There is still the good chance that the PS file itself is the problem.
The viewers rely on the PS files using the DSC (document structuring
conventions), if they are not there, they usually fall back to streammode.
And, of course, PS can contain evil code, as often seen with dvi2ps output...

You would not have any of this problems with a cheaper gfx, f.i. HX :-(
