There have been a lot of replies to this query debating the relative
merits of tar vs. dump.  For an initial snapshot of your system disk,
there's no substitute for a level 0 dump.

But for regularly scheduled backups with a mix of full/incrementals
and a user interface a little easier than cron/tar, I recommend
POLYCENTER NetWorker Save and Restore (old name was "DECnsr"). Does
file-based backups like tar, but gives a lot more control.  Can also
backup other networked UNIX client systems.

Unlike tar, cpio or dump, you DO have to buy a license to use it, but
IMHO, it's worth it in the long run.

Of course, I'm a little biased :-)

