re: backup strategies.

I try to keep mine simple:

1.  Make a full back of everything, with the system running
    single user.  Put these backups on a shelf.

	# dump 0u filesystem

2.  For every interesting file, make an incremental backup
    of everything that has changed since the last full
    backup.

	# dump 9u filesystem

3.  You can rotate the incremental tapes, so that "todays"
    backup doesn't overwrite "yesterdays" backup.  Use as
    many incremental tapes as you feel are necessary.

4.  Every so often I rotate in a new set of tapes for the
    full and incremental.

--
Alan Rollow				alan@nabeth.cxo.dec.com



