Examining my machine running 1.3 - no files in /etc are world writable.

I am not sure what you have in your root's .profile that bothers you
(except perhaps for /usr/local)

There is a utility you can run and look for consistancy errors in
permissions and files....

See the man page on fverify... You feed it as input the inventory for a
particular subset as stored in /usr/.smdb./*.inv

Make sure you use the one for the latest release that you have present
as old software release inventory files are kept there and not discarded
- but then the permissions and file listing are out of date and cannot
be tested.

You can run the program as yourself, but then programs which are not
readable by you (and only executable) will be listed as errors - but you
can probably live with that...

Good luck and have fun....

(On the side - the only security holes that I have heard about with 1.3
are something with crontab and the sendmail one which there is a patch
available)

	Ezra



