I guess it depends on what you mean. If you are talking about "off of the
tape" (meaning the R6 distribution) then that is still a matter of 
debate here at Digital.

If you mean support by Digital bundled with the OS, then yes, there is
a real reason to be optimistic. The numbers for the Hx and its replacement
card (know variously as Hx+, SFB+ and a half dozen other names) are quite
impressive, definitly competitive in the 2D workstation class of graphics.
(mileage varies depending on actual use, cpu clock speed, bus speed
and probably my mood :-).

The real question is how much of that hardware support will be folded back
to the XC in time for R6.

At a minimum, I think that non-accelerated HX code will be fed back. This
is probably similar to what you are seeing with the MX & HX under R5 and
Ultrix, basically just a dumb color frame buffer support.

If you have a compelling argument you want us to consider then please feel
free to either post in comp.unix.osf.osf1 or send me mail. Actually we/I
would like to hear any suggestions/comments on the X space. We can only
react to or consider customer requests when we hear of them.

/Dave (ddhill@zk3.dec.com)


