In article <2l13n1$42l@disun41.epfl.ch> monnier@di.epfl.ch (Stefan Monnier) writes:
>On my alpha here, I noticed that the automounter takes about 4% CPU
>time ("ps aux" dixit). And it actually varies more or less accordingly
>to dbx's cpu usage (always about half as much).
>
>My dbx is taking alot of CPU time (8%), but it's even worse for
>automount. Why is automount taking so much time ? 
>
>When does automount work ? Does it catch every single access to the
>mounted filesystem ?

Automount is invoked whenever someone does a lookup of a directory that is
mentioned in an automount map.  The lookup returns a symbolic link to the
real mount point of the file system, so further accesses should bypass the
automounter.

Does dbx have a list of directories it searches for source files?  If this
list contains absolute pathnames that go through automount points, then
every time it searches the directories it has to invoke the automounter.
