From george@ziggy.eng.miami.edu Wed Mar  2 14:55:02 1994
Subject: ghostview 1.5 error
To: wcwang@olympian.psych.indiana.edu

In case you have not gotten any answer yet:

grep the word "malformed" from the c-files. You will find it in a 
file named gdevxini.c. It is a error message that pops up when a 
condition is met, which precedes the line with the printf() message. 
The 'if' statement is incorrect. It has incorrect "and's" and "or's". 

The original block  reads:

 type == XA_STRING) {
            nitems = sscanf(buf, "%*s %d %d", &(xdev->foreground),
                                              &(xdev->background));
error!->     if (nitems != 2 || *buf != 'M' || *buf != 'G' || *buf != 'C') {
                eprintf("gs: Malformed ghostview color property.\n");
                exit(1);
            }
            palette = max(palette, *buf);

And it should read:

 type == XA_STRING) {
            nitems = sscanf(buf, "%*s %d %d", &(xdev->foreground),
                                              &(xdev->background));
fix ->      if (nitems != 2 || (*buf != 'M' && *buf != 'G' && *buf != 'C')) {
                eprintf("gs: Malformed ghostview color property.\n");
addition        eprintf2("gs: got \"%s\" (nitems=%d).\n", buf, nitems);
addition        eprintf("gs: expected \"%%*s %%d %%d\".\n");
                exit(1);
            }
            palette = max(palette, *buf);

 
Hope this helps.

Good luck.

George


