I posted this to the list wais-talk@think.com a week ago. I think the
changes below should be valid for freeWAIS 0.1 (which I think is equal to
wais-8b5.1).

Original posting:
==============================================================================
I downloaded FreeWAIS 0.202 from CNIDR some time ago, and have been trying
to make it to work on my Alpha off and on since then. With some help from
David Kulp <dkulp@gdb.org>, and a lot of help from Bernard Szelag
<Bernard.Szelag@univ-lille1.fr>, I think that I have sorted out most of the
problems involved in the port. Here is a list of things that I have changed
in the original CNIDR code to make it work on my Alpha.

The Alpha-specific changes are set by compiler flags, and the hard-coded
changes seems mostly to be bugs (?). Would it be possible to have someone
at CNIDR to look at this and maybe include these changes in the upcoming
code for freeWAIS 1.0, so we can make it compile easily on OSF1 when it
arrives?

If you have any questions about these changes, you may ask me, but don't
expect any clever answers, because Bernard Szelag is the one responsible
for the code analysis - I'm just reporting it (I can't C - yet :-).

OK, so here's the list:

1. The most important change seems to be the use of cc with -taso argument.

It compiles and loads with 32 bits pointers.

In the top Makefile:
CFLAGS = -O -taso -I$(SUPDIR) -DSECURE_SERVER -DRELEVANCE_FEEDBACK -DUSG
-DBOOLEANS -DPARTIALWORD -DLITERAL -DAXP

2. I had to define the compiler as ANSI_LIKE in the ir/cdialect.h file.
This can be done by adding a -DAXP compiler directive in the top Makefile:
CFLAGS = -O -taso -I$(SUPDIR) -DSECURE_SERVER -DRELEVANCE_FEEDBACK -DUSG
-DBOOLEANS -DPARTIALWORD -DLITERAL -DAXP

And then in ir/cdialect.h:
#ifdef AXP /* for 64 bits alpha risc processor */
#define ANSI_LIKE
#endif /* def AXP */

3. A math problem (division by zero? bug?) in ir/sersrch.c for the line:
weight/=doc_entry.document_length 
I think it was this one that made waissearch dump with a floating point
exception.
Should be changed to:
if (doc_entry.document_length != 0) weight/=doc_entry.document_length;

4. There are also some changes (which I don't understand) in ir/irsearch.c,
where (time_t)0L is changed to (time_t)0. See the diff listing below. Are
these typos?

5. In ir/trie.c, you have to change
   if (!(tmp->tries = make_allocator(sizeof(trie),free_trie))) {
to
   if (!(tmp->tries = make_allocator(sizeof(trie),(void *)free_trie))) {
(What does void mean in C ?)

6. In the lib/Makefile it seems as if the compiler flags from the top
Makefile are overridden by local CFLAGS. On recommendation from Bernard
Szelag, I commented them away.
#CFLAGS             = -DUSG -g  -I.

7 . In lib/pdftw.h, we have to make OSF known:
Change
#if defined(USG) || defined(_IBMR2)
to
#if defined(USG) || defined(_IBMR2) || defined(AXP)

8. The x/Imakefile:
Change
INCLUDES = -I$(SRCDIR) -I$(SUPDIR) -I$(UIDIR) -I/usr/openwin/include
to
INCLUDES = -I$(SRCDIR) -I$(SUPDIR) -I$(UIDIR)

9. The x/Imakefile: 
For 32 bits pointer under osf1.3 use a copy of LDOPTIONS and add -taso
LDOPTIONS = $(CDEBUGFLAGS) $(CCOPTIONS) $(LOCAL_LDFLAGS) -taso

10. In x/Xwais a lot of parameters pointing to local files have to be set. 
See the diff listing below.


Here is Bernard Szelag's "diff -r" between the original version and his
Alpha version:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
