Has anybody come upon that potential bug in the X library of OSF/1 1.3
on alpha:

It shows up with ctwm3.1beta if you use its animation option:
sometimes when ctwm wants to open a window (for some random client
like xterm), it might be prevented to do so for various reasons
(typically xlock, but it's not the only option). It normally just
waits until it can go on working, but from time to time, it just hangs
there, its virtual size getting bigger and bigger.

It's actually stuck in _XWaitForReadable which is called by _XReadPad,
called by XGetWindowProperty, called by XFetchName (called by ctwm).

This is not specific to an X server, but to the the alpha OSF1 version
of ctwm and it seems like the bug isn't in ctwm but in the X library
(the same code runs fine on Suns and other machines and also runs fine
on alpha as long as you don't use the animation option).

Does anybody know what could make the X library get stuck there ?


