We have a Ciper DLT 6 gbyte tape drive with 7 cartridge loader
connected to a Decstation 5000/240 that we use to backup all disk on
about 30 systems.

Until now we have not really looked at throughput but we are finding
that there are not enough hours during the weekend to complete a
complete level 0 dump.

We currently do dumps by a crontab entry on the tape host by a series
of commands of the form 

rsh diskhost rdump 0uf tapehost:/dev/rmt0h /filesystem

I have just looked at the timings and find the following throughputs in
Mbytes/min. (numbers in brackets is no of filesystems giving this
figure)

Local disks on tapehost                              30   (6)
Ethernet (10BaseT) connected Ultrix Hosts             3   (20)
Ethernet (10Base2) connected Ultrix Hosts             1.5 (2) ?
FDDI Connected Ultrix Hosts (system disk)             3   (6) 
FDDI Connected Ultrix Hosts ( non system disks)       6   (2) ?
Ethernet connected 3000/400 OSF/1                     3   (4)
Ethernet connected 3000/400 OSF/1                    10   (1) ?
FDDI connected 3000/400 OSF/1                        30   (1)

I cannot comment on the apparent inconsistancies in these figures
particularly those with (?) but these seem to be the real figures we get.

I would like to speed up all the remote systems and thought I would
have a look at the port of dump-restore by Marcus J Ranum but
decuac.dec.com appears unreachable. 

I did find a file dump_fast.tar by Paul Placeway on Gatekeeper.dec.com
has anyone any experience of this?

I would really appreciate any help to improve our throughput.

Other points I don't like about the dec dump are 

1) that if it encounters any error it sits there consuming all
available CPU cycles until killed - presumably asking a non-ex istent
terminal if it should continue or abort - hardly appropriate when run
from cron.  

2) does not return error status 

3) On reaching EOF I would like it to issue an mt offline so that next
tape would be automatically loaded.

4) Has the bug been fixed so that resore can read multiple volume dumps?

Many thanks for your help.
